pi05-infer

Extracted from RLinf (https://github.com/RLinf/RLinf) and built on openpi
(https://github.com/Physical-Intelligence/openpi, via the RLinf/openpi fork) and
HuggingFace Transformers. This product includes software developed by third
parties, redistributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

The files listed below are vendored copies or derivatives and carry their
original copyright notices in their headers; those notices are retained as
Apache-2.0 requires. Files original to this project carry the licence grant
without a copyright line.

================================================================================
Provenance: vendored code and per-file modifications
================================================================================

1. pi05_infer/gemma/modeling_gemma.py
   Derived from HuggingFace Transformers (`transformers/models/gemma/
   modeling_gemma.py`), Copyright 2024 Google Inc. and the HuggingFace Inc.
   team, Apache-2.0. The original copyright header is retained in the file.

   Modifications by this project, for bs=1 flow-matching inference of the
   pi0.5 action expert:
     - adaptive-RMSNorm modulation threaded as a precomputed tensor
       (`adarms_mod`) instead of a per-step per-layer projection;
     - fused QKV projection weight (`build_qkv_fused`);
     - static KV buffer for the frozen prefix (`prime_kv_static`), replacing
       a per-step `torch.cat`;
     - in-place refresh of weight-derived tensors (`refresh_derived_weights`);
     - optional fused GeGLU and fused QKV+RoPE fast paths dispatching to
       `rlinf_fused_denoise.py`, each guarded and falling back to the
       unmodified PyTorch path;
     - the package-relative imports of the original file rewritten to absolute
       `transformers.*` imports, so the file works outside the transformers
       package tree. Every symbol not listed above is imported from the
       installed transformers rather than copied.

2. pi05_infer/gemma/rlinf_fused_denoise.py
   New code written for this project: two Triton kernels exposed as
   `torch.library` custom ops (gate/up -> GeGLU epilogue; QKV -> RoPE
   epilogue writing into the static KV cache), each with a plain-PyTorch
   fallback.

3. pi05_infer/openpi_patched/{pi0_pytorch.py, gemma_pytorch.py}
   Derived from openpi (https://github.com/Physical-Intelligence/openpi),
   Apache-2.0, via the RLinf fork (https://github.com/RLinf/openpi).
   Modifications: NVTX instrumentation, batched multi-view SigLIP prefix
   embedding, on-device construction of the prefix attention mask (removing a
   host synchronisation), threading of the `adarms_mod` tensor, and building
   the action expert from `pi05_infer/gemma` while the PaliGemma prefix
   continues to use the installed transformers.

4. pi05_infer/_vendored/{base_policy.py, cuda_graph.py, nvtx.py}
   pi05_infer/dataconfig/, pi05_infer/engine.py, pi05_infer/builder.py
   Derived from RLinf (https://github.com/RLinf/RLinf), Apache-2.0.
   `engine.py` is an extraction of the pure-inference path from RLinf's
   `rlinf/models/embodiment/openpi/openpi_action_model.py`, with the
   reinforcement-learning instrumentation removed. `cuda_graph.py`,
   `dataconfig/policies/{turtle,libero}_policy.py` and
   `dataconfig/policies/__init__.py` are byte-identical to their RLinf
   originals; the other files in this group differ only as recorded in
   EXTRACTION_NOTES.md sections 2 to 4.

5. bench/standalone_infer_bench.py
   Derived from RLinf, Apache-2.0: adapted from RLinf's
   `benchmarks/pi05_infer/standalone_infer_bench.py` at rev `cbb9d2fc`.
   Only the model-construction seam changed -- the timing harness, dummy
   observation generator and phase decomposition are unchanged. Two optional
   flags (`--dump-actions`, `--clocks-json`) were added; both are no-ops
   unless passed.

6. _extract_src/{openpi_action_model.py, standalone_infer_bench.py}
   Verbatim, unmodified copies of RLinf sources at rev `cbb9d2fc`, Apache-2.0,
   kept only as the material that `pi05_infer/engine.py` and `bench/` were
   extracted from. Not part of the installed package and not importable; md5
   checksums are in `_extract_src/README.md`.

7. pi05_infer/patches/{__init__.py, inductor_mm_tiles.py, prefix_last_layer.py,
   prefix_qkv_fused.py}
   New code written for this project: optimizations applied at runtime to
   installed libraries rather than by forking them -- extra small-M tile
   candidates for torch inductor's `mm`/`bmm` templates, and two instance-level
   `forward` swaps on the stock-transformers PaliGemma prefix.

